urn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and the pull request is open with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it does banker's rounding. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` when the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`), I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **Pull request:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against `main`. The first attempt to open it failed with a temporary server error (503). I checked that no PR had been created, then retried with the same request key so it couldn't be created twice. There's exactly one open PR.\n\nThe PR isn't merged: merging into `main` needs a code owner's approval. Also, the lookup tool didn't recognise FIN-212, so I relied on the test and the docstring for the rounding requirement.", "type": "text"}]}]}